\fs20\insrsid4402984 The \endash  PICTURE character prints a minus sign only if the quantity is negative and omits a sign for all other quantities. It can appear as the leftmost or rightmost character. The \endash 
 PICTURE insertion character differs from the S character in that the use of the S character identifies a field as a signed one for computational purposes, but the sign does not occupy a position. Use of the \endash 
 PICTURE  character leads to a field in which the sign occupies a character position.
\par }\pard\plain \ltrpar\qj \li0\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid16136647 \rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs24\alang1025 \ltrch\fcs0 \fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs20 \ltrch\fcs0 
