\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0\afs32 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\fs32\ul\insrsid4402984 FILE SECTION.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs20 \ltrch\fcs0 \fs20\insrsid4402984 
\par }\pard \ltrpar\qj \fi720\li0\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid16136647 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs20 \ltrch\fcs0 \fs20\insrsid4402984 
Each file is described in the FILE SECTION with an FD sentence that may consist of a series of clauses. After the clauses are specified, the FD sentence ends with a period. FD is an abbreviation for File Description. Each FD entry will describe a file def
ined in a SELECT statement in the ENVIRONMENT DIVISION.
\par }\pard \ltrpar\qj \li0\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid16136647 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs20 \ltrch\fcs0 \fs20\insrsid4402984 \tab 
The two entries, DATA DIVISION and FILE SECTION, are coded in Area A. FD is also coded in Area A. The file-name, however, is typically coded in Area B. 
\par 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0\afs20 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\fs20\ul\insrsid4402984 Eg 8.2:
