\f1\fs20\insrsid4402984 DATA DIVISION.
\par FILE SECTION.
\par FD   EMPLOYEE-FILE
\par         LABEL RECORDS ARE STANDARD
\par          RECORD CONTAINS 70 CHARACTERS
\par           BLOCK CONTAINS 10 RECORDS.
\par }\pard \ltrpar\qj \li0\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid16136647 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs20 \ltrch\fcs0 \fs20\insrsid4402984 
\par }\pard\plain \ltrpar\s9\qj \li0\ri0\keepn\widctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\outlinelevel8\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid16136647 \rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0\afs28\alang1025 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\fs28\ul\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\rtlch\fcs1 
\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid4402984 Label Records
\par }\pard\plain \ltrpar\s59\qj \fi720\li0\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid16136647 \rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs24\alang1025 \ltrch\fcs0 \fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs20 \ltrch\fcs0 
\fs20\insrsid4402984 Label records are usually created as the first and last records of a disk or tape to provide identifying inform
ation about the file on disk or tape. Labels are created on output files so that, when the same file is later read as input, the labels may be checked to ensure that the file being accessed is the correct one. Labels are created on output files and checke
d on input files. The COBOL compiler will supply the routine for writing labels on output files or for checking labels on input file if the entry LABEL RECORDS ARE STANDARD is included.
\par }\pard\plain \ltrpar\qj \li0\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid16136647 \rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs24\alang1025 \ltrch\fcs0 \fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs20 \ltrch\fcs0 
\fs20\insrsid4402984 
\par This LABEL RECORDS clause will result in the following :
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\ltrpar \rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs20 \ltrch\fcs0 \fs20\lang1033\langfe1033\langnp1033\langfenp1033\insrsid4402984 \hich\af0\dbch\af0\loch\f0 1.\tab}}\pard \ltrpar\qj \fi-360\li720\ri0\widctlpar
\jclisttab\tx720\wrapdefault\faauto\ls16\adjustright\rin0\lin720\itap0\pararsid4728883 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs20 \ltrch\fcs0 \fs20\insrsid4402984 For output
 files, the first record on disk or tape file will be created as a standard 80-position header label identifying the file to the system; similarly, the last record on the disk or tape will be created as a trailer label.
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\ltrpar \rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs20 \ltrch\fcs0 \fs20\lang1033\langfe1033\langnp1033\langfenp1033\insrsid4402984 \hich\af0\dbch\af0\loch\f0 2.\tab}For input files, these labels wil
l be computer-checked to ensure that the file being processed is the correct one.
\par }\pard \ltrpar\qj \li0\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid16136647 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs20 \ltrch\fcs0 \fs20\insrsid4402984 
\par }\pard \ltrpar\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid16136647 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs20 \ltrch\fcs0 \fs20\insrsid4402984 
The clause LABEL RECORDS ARE STANDARD is permitted for disk and tape files only. Devices such as printers do not use label records, since identifying information is unnecess
ary where data is visible to the human eye. The clause LABEL RECORDS ARE OMITTED is used for such files.
\par }\pard \ltrpar\qj \li0\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid16136647 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs20 \ltrch\fcs0 \fs20\insrsid4402984 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0\afs28 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\fs28\ul\insrsid4402984 RECORD CONTAINS clause}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs20 \ltrch\fcs0 \fs20\insrsid4402984 
\par }\pard \ltrpar\qj \fi720\li0\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid16136647 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs20 \ltrch\fcs0 \fs20\insrsid4402984 
The RECORD CONTAINS clause indicates the size of each record. For printer files the RECORD CONTAINS clause may include one extr
a position that is used to control the spacing of the form (e.g., single spacing, double spacing). Thus, for 132 character printers, a record size is sometimes set as 133 characters. In such cases, the first or leftmost position in these 133-position prin
t records is the form control position; it is not actually printed.
\par }\pard \ltrpar\qj \li0\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid16136647 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs20 \ltrch\fcs0 \fs20\insrsid4402984 
\par 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0\afs28 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\fs28\ul\insrsid4402984 BLOCK CONTAINS clause}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs20 \ltrch\fcs0 \fs20\insrsid4402984 
\par }\pard \ltrpar\qj \fi720\li0\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid16136647 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs20 \ltrch\fcs0 \fs20\insrsid4402984 
The BLOCK CONTAINS clause is included in the File Description entry only for files in which disk or tape 
records have been blocked. Blocking is a technique that increases the speed of input/output operations and makes more effective use of storage space on disk and tape. A group of logical records is included within one block to maximize the efficient use of
 a disk or tape area. For example, reading in a block of 10 disk records, is more efficient than reading in each disk record separately. Even if blocking is used, the program processes records in the standard way, that is, one logical record at a time.

\par }\pard \ltrpar\qj \li0\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid16136647 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs20 \ltrch\fcs0 \fs20\insrsid4402984 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0\afs28 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\fs28\ul\insrsid4402984 Record Description entries}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs20 \ltrch\fcs0 \fs20\insrsid4402984 
\par }\pard \ltrpar\qj \fi720\li0\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid16136647 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs20 \ltrch\fcs0 \fs20\insrsid4402984 
A record is a unit of information consisting or related data items within a file. Most often, a file consists of records that all have the same length and format. These are called fixed-length records.
\par For each file defined, we have one record format.
\par }\pard \ltrpar\qj \li0\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid16136647 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs20 \ltrch\fcs0 \fs20\insrsid4402984 
