\par }\pard\plain \ltrpar\s9\qj \li0\ri0\keepn\widctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\outlinelevel8\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid16136647 \rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0\afs28\alang1025 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\fs28\ul\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\rtlch\fcs1 
\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid4402984 WRITE statement
\par }\pard\plain \ltrpar\qj \fi720\li0\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid16136647 \rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs24\alang1025 \ltrch\fcs0 \fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs20 \ltrch\fcs0 
\fs20\insrsid4402984 The WRITE instruction takes data in the output area defined in the DATA DIVISION and transmits it to the device specified in the ENVIRONMENT DIVISION. 
\par Note that although files are read, we write records. The record-name appear on the 01 level and is generally subdivided into fields. The record description specifies the format of the output.  
\par }\pard\plain \ltrpar\s9\qj \li0\ri0\keepn\widctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\outlinelevel8\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid16136647 \rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0\afs28\alang1025 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\fs28\ul\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\rtlch\fcs1 
\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid4402984 
\par }\pard\plain \ltrpar\qj \li0\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid16136647 \rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs24\alang1025 \ltrch\fcs0 \fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0\afs20 \ltrch\fcs0 
\b\fs20\ul\insrsid4402984 Eg 8.6:
\par }\pard \ltrpar\qj \li0\ri0\widctlpar\brdrt\brdrs\brdrw45\brsp20 \brdrl\brdrs\brdrw45\brsp80 \brdrb\brdrs\brdrw45\brsp20 \brdrr\brdrs\brdrw45\brsp80 \wrapdefault\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid16136647 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af1\afs20 \ltrch\fcs0 
\f1\fs20\insrsid4402984 WRITE  EMPLOYEE-REC.
\par }\pard\plain \ltrpar\s9\qj \li0\ri0\keepn\widctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\outlinelevel8\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid16136647 \rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0\afs28\alang1025 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\fs28\ul\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\rtlch\fcs1 
\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid4402984 
\par CLOSE statement
\par }\pard\plain \ltrpar\qj \fi720\li0\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid16136647 \rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs24\alang1025 \ltrch\fcs0 \fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs20 \ltrch\fcs0 
\fs20\insrsid4402984 A CLOSE statement is coded at the end of the job after all records have been processed to release these files and deact
ivate the devices. All files that have been opened at the beginning of the program are closed at the end of a program. The CLOSE statement, like the OPEN, will perform additional functions. When creating disk or tape records, for example, the CLOSE will c
reate trailer labels; it will also rewind a tape. 
\par }\pard \ltrpar\qj \li0\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid16136647 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs20 \ltrch\fcs0 \fs20\insrsid4402984 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0\afs20 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\fs20\ul\insrsid4402984 Eg 8.7:
\par }\pard \ltrpar\qj \li0\ri0\widctlpar\brdrt\brdrs\brdrw45\brsp20 \brdrl\brdrs\brdrw45\brsp80 \brdrb\brdrs\brdrw45\brsp20 \brdrr\brdrs\brdrw45\brsp80 \wrapdefault\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid16136647 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af1\afs20 \ltrch\fcs0 
\f1\fs20\insrsid4402984 CLOSE  EMPLOYEE-FILE.
\par }\pard \ltrpar\qj \li0\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid16136647 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs20 \ltrch\fcs0 \fs20\insrsid4402984 
\par 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0\afs32 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\fs32\ul\insrsid4402984 COPY statement
