\fs20\insrsid4402984 
With COBOL 74, the procedure-name of an INPUT PROCEDURE must be a section-name and not a paragraph-name. A section is a series of PROCEDURE DIVISION paragraphs that is treated as a single entry or unit. Rule for forming section-names are the s
ame as rules for forming paragraph-names. The word SECTION, however, follows a section-name (e.g., A000-ERROR SECTION). The end of a section is recognized when another section-name is encountered, or when the end of the program is reached. 
\par }\pard\plain \ltrpar\qj \li0\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid16136647 \rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs24\alang1025 \ltrch\fcs0 \fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs20 \ltrch\fcs0 
