\par {\listtext\pard\plain\ltrpar \s57 \rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs20 \ltrch\fcs0 \fs20\lang1033\langfe1033\langnp1033\langfenp1033\insrsid4402984 \hich\af0\dbch\af0\loch\f0 1.\tab}}\pard \ltrpar\s57\qj \fi-360\li720\ri0\widctlpar
\jclisttab\tx720\wrapdefault\faauto\ls19\adjustright\rin0\lin720\itap0\pararsid4728883 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs20 \ltrch\fcs0 \fs20\insrsid4402984 More than one ALTERNATE record key can be used.
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\ltrpar \s57 \rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs20 \ltrch\fcs0 \fs20\lang1033\langfe1033\langnp1033\langfenp1033\insrsid4402984 \hich\af0\dbch\af0\loch\f0 2.\tab}
WITH DUPLICATES means than an ALTERNATE RECORD KEY need not be unique. Thus, fields like EMP-DEPT can be used as a key even though numerous records may have the same department no.
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\ltrpar \s57 \rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs20 \ltrch\fcs0 \fs20\lang1033\langfe1033\langnp1033\langfenp1033\insrsid4402984 \hich\af0\dbch\af0\loch\f0 3.\tab}A record can be accessed by its RECORD KEY or any of its ALTERNATE RECORD KEYs.
\par }\pard \ltrpar\s57\qj \li0\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid16136647 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs20 \ltrch\fcs0 \fs20\insrsid4402984 
