he best method for searching a table is with the use of a SEARCH statement. The identifier used with the SEARCH verb is the table entry name specified on the OCCURS level, not on the 01 level. The WHEN clause indicates what action is to be taken when the 
condition specified is actually met. Additional comparisons between search and table arguments can be made using other WHEN clauses. The AT END  clause specifies what should be done if the table has been completely searched and no match is found. 
\par \tab To use a SEARCH statement, two additional entries are required : the INDEXED BY clause along with OCCURS, and the SET statement in the PROCEDURE DIVISION.
